// Skill cape equip gates.
//
// The level check passes the ALREADY-EVALUATED stat as an int rather than taking a 'stat'
// parameter. 'stat' is a real type in engine.rs2 command signatures, but no script in this repo
// passes one as a proc/label argument, so it is unproven here - whereas stat_base(attack) as an
// int argument is ordinary and cannot surprise the compiler.
//
// Hoods are cosmetic and ungated, matching the live game.

[label,skillcape_require](int $level, string $skill, int $slot)
if ($level < 99) {
    mes("You need level 99 <$skill> to wear this cape.");
    return;
}
~equip($slot);

// Hunter does not exist on this server, so its cape is imported but cannot be worn. Construction
// used to be here too and no longer is - the skill landed, so the cape did. Replace this with a
// real skillcape_require call if Hunter ever arrives, and add it to the stats enum in the same
// breath: the Max cape's requirement and Mac's price are both counted out of that enum.
[label,skillcape_unavailable](string $what)
mes("<$what> is not available on this server yet, so this cape cannot be worn.");

// THE MAX CAPE: level 99 in every skill there is. "Every skill there is" is the stats enum - 22 of
// them, Construction included since the houses landed, Hunter excluded because this server has no
// Hunter - so the gate is a count rather than a list of names and follows the enum on its own.
[opheld2,max_cape]
if (~skillcape_count_99s < enum_getoutputcount(stats)) {
    mes("You need level 99 in all <tostring(enum_getoutputcount(stats))> skills to wear the Max cape.");
    return;
}
~equip(last_slot);

[opheld2,attack_cape] @skillcape_require(stat_base(attack), "Attack", last_slot);
[opheld2,attack_cape_t] @skillcape_require(stat_base(attack), "Attack", last_slot);
